# The published documentation site, assembled by `.github/workflows/docs.yml` from the reference,
# the module pages and rustdoc. Built on every run; never checked in. What *is* checked in is
# `docs/reference/`, the markdown the drift gate compares against (docs/adr/0007).
site/

# `beck doc module <file>` with no `--out` writes here, and a test binary's working directory is its
# crate. Nothing reads these pages — the published site is assembled into `site/` above — so they
# are output rather than source, and were checked in for several commits before anybody noticed
# (`beck-cli/tests/stdlib.rs::every_library_documents` passes `--stdout` now).
compiler/crates/beck-cli/doc/

# `release/build.sh`'s output: a tarball and its checksum, per target. Built by the release
# workflow and uploaded to the release; never checked in (docs/92 §92.8).
dist/
